</div><div class="html-p">In terms of energy and throughput, the Q4_K_M configurations—particularly the Ministral 3 3B Instruct–Q4_K_M and the Nemotron 3 Nano 4B–Q4_K_M—stood out from the other configurations in all three generation scenarios. Ministral–Q4_K_M combined the lowest dynamic energy per token with the highest throughput, while Nemotron–Q4_K_M used less GPU memory. The Relationship Between Dynamic Energy and Throughput, and the Pareto Fronts in TG-256, PG-512/256, and PG-2048/256 are shown in <a href="#energies-19-04893-f001" class="html-fig">Figure 1</a>. This figure shows a two-dimensional projection of the Pareto set obtained using all four criteria. Non-dominated configurations were identified separately for each workload scenario based on four criteria: dynamic energy consumption per processed token (minimized), generation throughput (maximized), peak GPU memory usage (minimized), and average GPU power consumption (minimized). A configuration was considered Pareto-optimal if no other evaluated configuration performed at least as well across all four criteria while achieving a strictly better result in at least one of them.</div><div class="html-fig-wrap" id="energies-19-04893-f001" data-position="float"><button type="button" class="html-media-expand" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path fill="currentColor" d="M3 21v-8h2v4.6L17.6 5H13V3h8v8h-2V6.4L6.4 19H11v2z"></path></svg></button>
