</div><div class="html-p">Across all four model families, Q4_K_M showed significantly lower dynamic GPU energy per token and higher generation throughput than BF16. Depending on the model and scenario, Q4_K_M reduced the average dynamic energy per token by 63.6–85.7% and increased generation throughput by 85.2–160.2%. All 24 Q4_K_M–BF16 comparisons for energy and throughput remained significant after Holm correction (<span class="html-italic">p<sub>Holm</sub></span> ≤ 0.0041).</div><div class="html-p">The largest relative reduction in energy consumption was observed for the Ministral 3 3B Instruct, for which Q4_K_M consumed 84.0–85.7% less energy per token than BF16. At the same time, the throughput of this configuration was 105.2–160.2% higher. The very large effect sizes reflected both large differences in means and low variability within most configurations. <a href="#energies-19-04893-t003" class="html-table">Table 3</a>, <a href="#energies-19-04893-t004" class="html-table">Table 4</a>, <a href="#energies-19-04893-t005" class="html-table">Table 5</a> and <a href="#energies-19-04893-t006" class="html-table">Table 6</a> present the results of the analyses.</div><div class="html-table-wrap" id="energies-19-04893-t003" data-position="float"><button type="button" class="html-media-expand" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path fill="currentColor" d="M3 21v-8h2v4.6L17.6 5H13V3h8v8h-2V6.4L6.4 19H11v2z"></path></svg></button>
